# Vendored font assets are byte-pinned to their upstream hashes (see
# design `2026-07-17-render-design-tokens` § Vendoring pin).
# `-text` disables EOL normalisation: without it, a `core.autocrlf` set in any
# contributor's personal ~/.gitconfig can rewrite an OFL.txt's CRLF endings at
# `git add` time, silently breaking its SHA-256 pin and the OFL's
# redistribution requirement. Face-independent — applies to every vendored
# font subdirectory, not just the one that first motivated it.
crates/render/fonts/** -text

# Vendored Lucide icon assets (SVG source + ISC LICENSE) are byte-pinned to
# their upstream SHA-256 (see design `2026-07-18-render-svg-icon-pipeline`
# § Licensing + vendoring). `-text` disables EOL normalisation for the same
# reason as the fonts block above: without it a contributor's `core.autocrlf`
# rewrites the SVG/LICENSE EOLs at `git add` time, breaking the SHA-256 pin and
# the exact-text ISC redistribution. `-text` (store bytes as downloaded from the
# pinned Lucide tag), not `text eol=lf`.
crates/render/icons/** -text
